lee-widgets.js: built from frontend/widgets.js and frontend/widgets.css in a scratch folder outside the repository, so no node tooling enters it. Packages, exact: @jupyter-widgets/html-manager@1.0.15 @jupyter-widgets/base@6.0.12 @jupyter-widgets/controls@5.0.13 @jupyter-widgets/output@6.0.12 esbuild@0.28.1 (node 26.5.0, npm 11.17.0).

    d=$(mktemp -d) && cp frontend/widgets.js frontend/widgets.css "$d" && cd "$d"
    npm init -y && npm install --save-exact @jupyter-widgets/html-manager@1.0.15 @jupyter-widgets/base@6.0.12 @jupyter-widgets/controls@5.0.13 @jupyter-widgets/output@6.0.12 esbuild@0.28.1
    node_modules/.bin/esbuild widgets.css --bundle --loader:.woff2=empty --loader:.woff=empty --loader:.ttf=empty --loader:.eot=empty --loader:.svg=empty --outfile=widgets.built.txt
    node_modules/.bin/esbuild widgets.js --bundle --format=iife --global-name=LeeWidgets --minify --loader:.txt=text --loader:.svg=text --loader:.css=empty --external:@jupyter-widgets/base7 --external:@jupyter-widgets/controls7 --outfile=lee-widgets.js
    cp lee-widgets.js <repo>/leela/vendor/ && cp node_modules/@fortawesome/fontawesome-free/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff2 <repo>/leela/vendor/fonts/

fonts/fa-solid-900.woff2 and fonts/LICENSE-Font-Awesome.txt: @fortawesome/fontawesome-free@5.15.4, the version html-manager 1.0.15 depends on.

lee-rupaka.js and lee-rupaka.css: rupaka 0.0.7 from PyPI, wheel rupaka-0.0.7-py3-none-any.whl, SHA-256 6beeebc98e17dd2d25205c6fcb08feb7799d31aa819b37848099e531dbd8f28b. Download the wheel into an empty folder, check the digest, then write the two bundles with the wheel's own renderer:

    d=$(mktemp -d) && curl -sS -o "$d/rupaka-0.0.7-py3-none-any.whl" https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/40/5c/5745e721b416ab9acb4e730a1607fef44ea0fa3abce0b2102658f9854de8/rupaka-0.0.7-py3-none-any.whl && shasum -a 256 "$d/rupaka-0.0.7-py3-none-any.whl"
    uv run --no-project --with "$d/rupaka-0.0.7-py3-none-any.whl" python -I -c 'import sys;from pathlib import Path;from rupaka.render import bundle;o=Path(sys.argv[1]);(o/"lee-rupaka.js").write_text(bundle("js"));(o/"lee-rupaka.css").write_text(bundle("css"))' leela/vendor

katex/: katex@0.16.47 from the npm registry, tarball katex-0.16.47.tgz, SHA-256 ad2d1ab2f7fcc227019784320e8a2c5218ff6bb333b36df4136d10365ae29375 (the registry's own sha1 0a13a42c2deb4f74e61f162d440b9165a548030f and sha512 Eeo8Ys1doU1z+x8AZsPpQu+p/QcZBI5PeOo7QGQdy2x2m0MU/hYagBbGOmXwr5KVbEfVuWv9LpnQWeehogurjg== both match). Download into an empty folder, check the digests, extract into another, and copy dist/katex.min.js, dist/katex.min.css and dist/fonts/*.woff2 (the stylesheet lists woff and ttf after woff2; no browser Leela runs in fetches them) with LICENSE as LICENSE-KaTeX.txt:

    d=$(mktemp -d) && curl -sS -o "$d/katex-0.16.47.tgz" https://registry.npmjs.org/katex/-/katex-0.16.47.tgz && shasum -a 256 "$d/katex-0.16.47.tgz"
    e=$(mktemp -d) && tar -xzf "$d/katex-0.16.47.tgz" -C "$e" && mkdir -p leela/vendor/katex/fonts && cp "$e/package/dist/katex.min.js" "$e/package/dist/katex.min.css" leela/vendor/katex/ && cp "$e"/package/dist/fonts/*.woff2 leela/vendor/katex/fonts/ && cp "$e/package/LICENSE" leela/vendor/katex/LICENSE-KaTeX.txt

