lee-texparts.js, lee-board.js, lee-board.css, board/rough.js and board/perfect-freehand.mjs: the screen guide's formula parts and board, copied unchanged from abhyasa commit 32b19de on branch v0015, which becomes abhyasa 0.0.15. abhyasa 0.0.15 is not on PyPI yet. At its release, copy the files from its wheel, record the wheel and its SHA-256 here in the form the 0.0.14 line used, and pin abhyasa to it; until then tests/test_vendor_board.py fails. The source files are abhyasa/core/texparts.js, abhyasa/core/board.js, abhyasa/core/board.css, abhyasa/core/vendor/rough.js and abhyasa/core/vendor/perfect-freehand.mjs. pyproject.toml pins abhyasa to this wheel. tests/test_vendor_board.py compares each file with the file in the installed wheel. board/ is the folder the page passes to the board as `host.assets`, served at /leestatic/board/. board/LICENSES.md is abhyasa's licence file for the two libraries. Download the wheel into an empty folder, check the digest, extract it into another folder, then copy the files:

    d=$(mktemp -d) && curl -sS -o "$d/abhyasa-0.0.14-py3-none-any.whl" https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/7c/5f/4d8e12fa2736c99f8a0a07d50937cca5e5b86bff1ac510d549f29dfd3744/abhyasa-0.0.14-py3-none-any.whl && shasum -a 256 "$d/abhyasa-0.0.14-py3-none-any.whl"
    e=$(mktemp -d) && unzip -q "$d/abhyasa-0.0.14-py3-none-any.whl" -d "$e" && c="$e/abhyasa/core" && cp "$c/texparts.js" leela/vendor/lee-texparts.js && cp "$c/board.js" leela/vendor/lee-board.js && cp "$c/board.css" leela/vendor/lee-board.css && cp "$c/vendor/rough.js" "$c/vendor/perfect-freehand.mjs" "$c/vendor/LICENSES.md" leela/vendor/board/

